<%# The spec asks for a remaining amount that is always visible, so it reads the
    same whether it is zero or not: the organizer should never have to wonder
    whether the line is missing or the figure is nil.

    What it is, said plainly: the part of the bill nobody has been asked for,
    which is the part the organizer is paying themselves. $100 with $20 asked of
    one person and $30 of another leaves "You pay $50.00".

    "Over the bill by" is the error state — unreachable by dragging, because a
    dragged row is clamped, but possible if the total is lowered underneath
    amounts that were already set. SplitLogic updates both on every drag. %>
<% remaining_cents = split.remaining_cents %>

<div id="remaining" class="mt-4 border-t-2 border-line pt-3">
  <p class="flex items-baseline justify-between">
    <span class="font-medium" data-split-logic-target="remainingLabel">
      <%= remaining_cents.negative? ? "Over the bill by" : "You pay" %>
    </span>
    <span class="font-medium tabular-nums" data-split-logic-target="remaining">
      <%= money(remaining_cents.abs) %>
    </span>
  </p>

  <% if split.custom? %>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
      Whatever you don't ask anyone for is yours to cover.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>
